# Pre-review gate

When you are the **implement** runtime about to move a Linear issue to `In Review`:

1. Rebase/merge `origin/<lanes.integration>` until `gh pr view --json mergeable` is
   `MERGEABLE`.
2. Run the full test graph. A targeted filter is not a substitute.
3. Wait for **all** required GitHub checks, including image/deploy smokes — not only
   `test`. Pending → do not flip status.
4. If you added a required boot env, grep every workflow that starts that process.
5. Spawn matching domain helpers. Read `docs/design-system.md` before UI and the
   architecture lock before Nest/auth.
6. On resume, fix the **class**, not only the cited file.

Do not call `/code-review` as the pass verdict — checker owns that in a fresh VM.

When you are the **checker**: every pass is a complete review of the current diff.
Dump every hard finding in this fail. Do not drip-feed.
